ocytosis and constitutional symptoms are more consistent with myeloproliferative or infectious process", "Post-viral syndrome: recent cold history is insufficient to explain persistent constitutional symptoms and leukemoid count"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Fever (37.5°C)", "Marked leukocytosis >65,000/mm³"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.23177257525083608, "posterior": 0.13213213213213212, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Weight loss and fever are concerning for malignancy but do not strongly exclude Leukemoid Reaction (B5). The result slightly reduces B5's probability."], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP is less specific for malignancy in non-infectious settings but still weakly supports a non-malignant process. This weakly favors B5."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.035, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["A normal differential strongly argues against ALL (B2), which typically presents with blasts. This result decisively excludes B2."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4056020066889631, "posterior": 0.4624624624624624, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP is more consistent with CML (B3) than Leukemoid 